  "id": "COMPOUND:28492 - PROTEIN:5943",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine may interact with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. This compound appears to act as a target for multiple compounds, including Ginsenoside R10, Neridienone A, and 6-C-Methylquercetin 3-methyl ether, all of which are known to target the VMRC-LCP protein. Since VMRC-LCP is a known target of these compounds, it is plausible that Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine exerts its effects through a similar mechanism, possibly by modulating VMRC-LCP activity. The consistent presence of VMRC-LCP as a common intermediate in these pathways supports the hypothesis that Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine may influence the activity of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP through the regulation of VMRC-LCP. The evidence is robust and aligns with a mechanistic framework that links the compound to the target protein via a shared pathway.",
